  {
   "n": 10,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>A 0-20V Range Dual Slope integrating type DMM is used to measure a DC Voltage of 10 V which&nbsp;has picked up a ac signal whose frequency is 50 Hz. The DMM has Four and half digit Display.&nbsp;The first integration period is set as 40 msec. What will be the reading of Voltmeter?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>20.000 V</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>10.000 V</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>19.999 V</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>09.999 V</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>Dual slope DMM measures average value since it integrates the signal under measurement. So,&nbsp;the average value is 10 V indicated on digital display as 10.000 V.</p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 11,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>The faulty ammeter in secondary of a current transformer (C.T) is replaced by</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>Open circuit the secondary of the C.T and replace it.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>Never short circuit the secondary of C.T while primary is energized.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>A short circuiting link is provided on secondary for replacing the faulty ammeter.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>It is not possible with out interrupting the line supply.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>When secondary of CT is made open but primary carrying current, the secondary MMF developed&nbsp;is zero. As secondary MMF is zero the primary MMF will be used to produced large flux which&nbsp;induces high emf, but the insulation of CT is not able to with stand such high voltages. A short<br>circuiting link is provided on secondary for replacing the faulty ammeter so that primary MMF is&nbsp;balanced by secondary MMF.</p>"
  },
